@startuml EcoLoop_MCP_Tools
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName IBM Plex Sans

title EcoLoop — MCP tool registry & tools\n(one MCP-compatible server module → five tools → LLM tool-calling)

package "MCP-compatible server layer" as MCP #EEF2FF {
  component "agent/mcp_server.py\n«MCP tool registry»\nMCP_TOOLS + Pydantic schemas" as REG

  package "Write tools (primary)" as W #ECFDF5 {
    usecase "set_hvac_setpoint\ncooling + heating °C\nper zone" as T1
    usecase "set_lighting_level\nlights 0.0–1.0\nper zone" as T2
  }

  package "Read / reason tools (optional)" as R #FEF3C7 {
    usecase "read_sensors\nzone temp, occ, CO2,\nsetpoints, outdoor, energy" as T3
    usecase "get_energy_report\nkWh, demand, savings\nvs baseline" as T4
    usecase "predict_comfort\nPMV for proposed\ncooling setpoint" as T5
  }
}

package "Runtime" as RT #F8FAFC {
  component "agent/tools.py\nToolExecutor" as EXEC
  component "agent/llm_client.py\nmcp_to_openai_tool()" as CONV
  component "agent/orchestrator.py" as ORCH
  component "LLM (Groq Llama)" as LLM
}

package "Building I/O" as IO #ECFDF5 {
  component "EPReader" as READ
  component "EPWriter + clamps" as WRITE
  component "comfort.pmv" as PMV
}

REG --> T1
REG --> T2
REG --> T3
REG --> T4
REG --> T5

ORCH --> EXEC : get_tool_definitions()
EXEC --> REG : MCP_TOOLS
ORCH --> CONV : offer tools each LLM step
CONV --> LLM : OpenAI function-calling format
LLM --> ORCH : tool_calls (model chooses)
ORCH --> EXEC : execute(name, args)

EXEC --> T1
EXEC --> T2
EXEC --> T3
EXEC --> T4
EXEC --> T5

T1 --> WRITE
T2 --> WRITE
T3 --> READ
T4 --> READ
T5 --> PMV

note right of REG
  **One logical MCP server**
  Not a separate multi-process
  MCP daemon — schemas live in
  mcp_server.py and are converted
  to OpenAI tools at call time.
end note

note bottom of LLM
  Trigger: LLM cadence steps only.
  Model decides which tool to call.
  Prompt steers toward T1 + T2.
end note

@enduml
